{"id": "DfZWYT6RY1g", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Bhishma, Drona and Karna all learned from ONE guru: Parshurama. One fought him, one got everything, one lied to him 🪓 Part 8, the finale of the Parshurama series.\n\nBHISHMA: When Parshurama ordered him to take back princess Amba, Bhishma said no, even to his own guru. They fought at Kurukshetra for 23 days. When Bhishma raised a weapon of sleep, Narada stopped him: \"He is your guru!\" Parshurama's own ancestors made him lay down his bow, and he told his student: \"No warrior on earth is your equal.\"\n\nDRONA: He came to Mahendra mountain when Parshurama had already given everything away, his gold to brahmins and the whole earth to Kashyapa. \"Only my body and my weapons are left. Choose.\" Drona said: \"All your weapons.\" And he got them.\n\nKARNA: \"I am a brahmin of Bhrigu's line,\" he said, and learned the Brahmastra. One day his guru slept with his head on Karna's lap, and an insect bored into his thigh. Karna didn't move, so his guru could sleep. The blood woke Parshurama: \"No brahmin could bear this pain. Who are you?\" \"Karna, son of Radha.\" \"You learned it with a lie. When you face your equal, you will forget it. Go. But no warrior on earth will be your equal.\"\n\nYears later, at Kurukshetra, all three led the same army, one after another, and all three fell there. And Parshurama? The Bhagavata says he still lives on Mahendra mountain. His next student, Kalki, isn't born yet.\n\n📖 Sources: Mahabharata, Udyoga Parva 180–188 (Bhishma), Adi Parva 131 (Drona), Shanti Parva 2–3 (Karna); Bhagavata Purana 9.16.26 (Mahendra); Kalki Purana (Kalki).\n\n📚 Stories of Shakti for little ones: the Navadurga Set from Rishi Katha is out now. Check the link in bio (rishikatha.com).\n\n💬 Who was his greatest student: Bhishma, Drona or Karna? Comment 👇\n🔁 Missed a part? All 8 parts of the Parshurama series are on our page. Save this one and share it with a Mahabharata fan.\n\n#parshuram #parshurama #karna #bhishma #dronacharya #mahabharata #kurukshetra #kalki #hindumythology #sanatandharma #indianmythology #mythologystories #rishikatha #hinduism #mahabharat", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793959558, "like_count": 25363, "comment_count": 105, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1150540250768100a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 50.239, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNuZpFZiNRevaWOxuhdJ_TfMyYib9SXOkMJXBCGXIIWpkxM4yA7qHGtjCiZlahxkXpakXZJPmyLfho7_rWtwFMFFEwIjbUc1bVyTpc.mp4?_nc_cat=106&_nc_oc=Adq0Uh8vlt2HTb1oRQOzQAHyLucUSQt4DR9JxmtDNdyPCKL8zjIxUXuKq4nYekX85LwifQcpRhwgjD2REf1v9H05&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=THmIKc5cxtgQ7kNvwGPYlMn&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=kgTsAK0IjL_zeHGntMrcUA&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQSnWCX1TY1P9WA1ccSPc3P_gfk-5fFlDdd6TARtQhgBfw&oe=6AF42D9B", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "audio_ext": "m4a", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 50.239, "resolution": "audio only", "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/150.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "format": "dash-1150540250768100a - audio only (DASH audio)"}, {"url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m86/AQNYzCamYGz4da7-y7cmvw_yQ_cup2IoE3zY64smyXuIIrQzEMam8RtA38d_CMF4ZOdNjQVSxKA4aMNRgm2osUbZlBbXGnj8ZDOLW-Y.mp4?_nc_cat=102&_nc_oc=AdpaOn7jzMqPKX7gABnWvORSfNQgvlNI4hv3M6fda0cpBzdH5M9TrOw1oS6ZUkY28SYgvxubd6V6cIYsdMtF2QLP&_nc_sid=5e9851&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=pY